msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4836
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"automatic-playlist-generator\">Automatic Playlist Generator</"
"link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4838
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Saved Playlists</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4839
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Saved playlist</emphasis> is a traditional type of playlist. Saved "
"playlists work like &amarok;'s current playlist, saved in the "
"<emphasis>Amarok Database</emphasis> or your file system for later use. "
"Sharing your saved playlists with your friends is easy and it can be fun to "
"use them at events when you have specific songs you want played."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4841
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Saved playlists can be created with &amarok; or imported from your file "
"system. Creating a saved playlist is very easy with the exact songs and "
"order that you want. For every day use, sometimes it is faster to use <link "
"linkend=\"dynamic-playlists\">Dynamic Playlists</link> or the <link linkend="
"\"automatic-playlist-generator\">Automatic Playlist Generator</link> when "
"you have less specific needs for specific tracks and progression."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4843
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To browse and manage your saved playlists, go to "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Playlists</guimenu><guimenuitem>Saved Playlists</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> on the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4845
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing saved playlists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4846
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saving a Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4860
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can save your current playlist into the <emphasis>Amarok database</"
"emphasis> by clicking the <guilabel>Save</guilabel> icon ( <screenshot> "
"<screeninfo></screeninfo> <mediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata fileref="
"\"playlist_save_icon_amarok.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject> "
"<textobject> <phrase></phrase> </textobject> </mediaobject> </screenshot>) "
"at the bottom of the <emphasis>Playlist</emphasis> view. You can browse "
"playlists in the <emphasis>Amarok database</emphasis> by going to "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Playlists</guimenu><guimenuitem>Saved Playlists</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> and expanding the <emphasis>Amarok database</"
"emphasis> section. You will find them in your filesystem here: <filename>~/."
"kde(4)/share/apps/amarok/playlists</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4874
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exporting a Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4875
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can export your current playlist to your file system by clicking "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Playlist</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export Playlist As...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the top menubar. From the opening save "
"dialog, you can change the name, location and type of the playlist. Then "
"just click on <guilabel>Save</guilabel>. Remember, playlist files don't "
"contain any music data. If you want to listen the content of the playlist on "
"another computer, you'll need to bring your music with you unless that "
"computer already has the tracks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4878
#, no-c-format
msgid "Importing a Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4879
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can import a playlist file into &amarok; just by copying it to any "
"directory that &amarok; knows as part of your music collection. When "
"&amarok; detects a new playlist on any folder of your collection, it will "
"add it to the <guilabel>Playlist Files on Disk</guilabel> section. If the "
"playlist doesn't appear right away, you can update the collection manually "
"by clicking <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Update "
"Collection</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. If instead of importing the playlist, "
"you want to just listen it, open it with <menuchoice><guimenu>Amarok</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Play Media...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from menubar. "
"Selected playlist will be added to the current playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4884
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist Filtering"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4885
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Search playlist</emphasis> function in &amarok; is very "
"powerful, as it allows you to search for different tracks by various "
"constraints. The search results limits what you can actually see, which "
"makes it easy to queue up wanted tracks, or remove them from the playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4901
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you type something in the field, &amarok; will search in your playlist "
"and mark matching tracks, artists and so forth."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
