#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5033
#, no-c-format
msgid "Queue Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5034
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tracks are loaded in the <emphasis>Playlist</emphasis>. In normal track "
"progression, when a song is over, the next one played is the one below the "
"just-played one. The <emphasis>Queue</emphasis> is one way to change the "
"order in which the songs are played."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5036
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Create a Queue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5037
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is very easy to make a <emphasis>Queue</emphasis>; just select one or "
"more tracks and move in the center of &amarok;, to the <emphasis>Pop-Up "
"Dropper</emphasis> (PUD), or right-click and scroll to <guilabel>Queue "
"Track</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5039
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you select or add songs to the <emphasis>Queue</emphasis> each of them "
"takes a number. The number indicates the order in which songs will play."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:5050
#, no-c-format
