#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5186
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Dynamic Playlists</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some media players are designed to load the entire collection of music in a "
"single playlist, then play it in random order, or search/ sorted, then "
"queued. With a larger collection, this way of managing your playlist isn't "
"efficient. &amarok;<command>'s</command> <emphasis>Dynamic Playlist</"
"emphasis> is a better way to explore your music."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Dynamic Playlist</emphasis> is reached from "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Playlists</guimenu><guimenuitem>Dynamic Playlists</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> in the <emphasis>Media Sources</emphasis> pane."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These instructions are for the new version of the dynamic playlist in Amarok "
"2.4.2 and above. See below for 2.4.1 and older."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5206
#, no-c-format
msgid "How the Dynamic Playlist works"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The dynamic playlist is a list that grows while you listen to your music."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It will keep a certain number of songs in front of the currently played song "
"and it will clean up the playlist by removing old songs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The songs that will be added to the front of the playlist are determined by "
"the currently selected dynamic playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5214
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a Dynamic Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enable dynamic playlists, click the <guilabel>Turn dynamic playlist on</"
"guilabel> button (the one with the small dice) in the dynamic playlist pane. "
"A bar will be displayed at the top of the playlist pane announcing that it "
"is enabled. Select which dynamic playlist to use from the list of options by "
"double clicking it. The currently selected dynamic playlist is bolded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can adjust the number of songs before and after the currently playing "
"song to be displayed in the playlist with the <guilabel>Previous</guilabel> "
"and <guilabel>Upcoming</guilabel> fields. You can prevent the same track "
"appearing in the current playlist more than once using the <guilabel>Allow "
"duplicate songs in result</guilabel> button. The <guilabel>Repopulate</"
"guilabel> button allows you to generate a new set of tracks. This can be "
"used together with a high <guilabel>Upcoming</guilabel> setting to generate "
"fixed playlists for export."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defining Dynamic Playlists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each dynamic playlist is built of biases. A bias defines a particular "
"constraint on the behaviour of the dynamic playlist, and new items to be "
"added to the playlist are selected at random from a list of all songs which "
"match the biases. Biases may either be a single bias (&eg; the "
"<emphasis>Search</emphasis> bias) or a grouping of other biases (&eg; the "
"<emphasis>Match All</emphasis> bias). Some examples playlists are included, "
"and you can define a new playlist with the <guilabel>New playlist</guilabel> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the name of a playlist, either use the <guilabel>Edit the selected "
"playlist or bias</guilabel> button or right click on it and select "
"<guilabel>Rename playlist</guilabel>. A bias can be edited with the same "
"button or by right-clicking and selecting <guilabel>Edit bias</guilabel>, "
"and for biases which have sub-biases, a new sub-bias can be added by right "
"clicking and selecting <guilabel>Add new bias</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5225 index.docbook:5322
#, no-c-format
msgid "Biases"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5226
#, no-c-format
msgid "An explanation of each available bias and any options it takes follows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5229
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>Search</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bias matches tracks found by a given search query. It uses the same "
"search string used in the collection browser. You may also use the "
"<emphasis>Match meta tag</emphasis> bias to match tags in the same way as "
"the collection search editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5234
#, no-c-format
msgid "Random"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5236
#, no-c-format
msgid "This bias matches any track, entirely at random."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5239
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>And</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group bias matches tracks which match <emphasis>all</emphasis> sub-"
"biases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5244
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>Or</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group bias matches tracks which match <emphasis>any</emphasis> sub-"
"biases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Partition"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group bias matches tracks from the sub-biases in proportion. The edit "
"window for this bias has sliders for each sub-bias to adjust the "
"proportions. For example, with two sub-biases with their proportion sliders "
"set equal, half of the playlist will match one bias and half the other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note: The dynamic playlist is internally working with more tracks than you "
"can see, so after clicking <quote>refresh</quote> the list might not contain "
"a 50:50 distribution of songs. However as you continue listening to music "
"you will see that in the end it actually matches."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5255
#, no-c-format
msgid "If Else"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group bias matches tracks from the first sub bias <emphasis>unless</"
"emphasis> there are no matching tracks found, in which case it matches "
"tracks from the second sub-bias. See the example Album Play playlist for an "
"example of this in use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Match Meta Tag"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bias matches tracks which meet certain conditions on a tag. The "
"selection interface is the same as the search filter editor in the "
"collection browser. Select a tag type from the drop-down and fill in the "
"constraint. (Hint: You can use a number of these in an <emphasis>And</"
"emphasis> bias.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Album Play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bias matches tracks related to the previous item in the playlist by "
"album. You can select the details of the bias from the drop-down menu. For "
"example, <quote>Track directly follows previous track in album</quote> is "
"used in the example Album Play playlist to ensure full albums are played in "
"order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5270
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quiz Play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bias matches tracks for which the first character of a given tag "
"(title, artist or album) is the same as the last character of the same tag "
"for the previous tag. For example, with artist selected, you could have the "
"following series: Led Zeppeli<guilabel>n</guilabel> -&gt; <guilabel>N</"
"guilabel>ine Inch Nail<guilabel>s</guilabel> -&gt; <guilabel>S</"
"guilabel>antana, e.t.c."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5275
#, no-c-format
msgid "EchoNest similar artist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bias matches tracks which are similar according to EchoNest, either to "
"the previous track or to any track in the playlist. This allows you to play "
"a set of consistent tracks simply by adding a single track to the playlist "
"and turning on the dynamic playlist, rather than defining all the match "
"rules yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5280
#, no-c-format
msgid "Last.fm similar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bias performs the same function as the EchoNest bias, but uses Last.fm "
"to determine similarity. You can also choose similarity to the previous "
"track or to the previous artist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:5285
#, no-c-format
msgid "Last.fm weekly top artist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bias matches tracks which are on the weekly charts from Last.fm for a "
"given time period."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5293 index.docbook:5351
#, no-c-format
msgid "A dynamic playlist in use"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5308
#, no-c-format
msgid "Old (2.4.1 and earlier) Dynamic Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Biases are what makes your dynamic playlist special! The default value for "
"the dynamic playlist, with no biases, is random play. Biases of various "
"sorts will alter that in different ways."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5326
#, no-c-format
msgid "Proportional Bias"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Proportional biases match a certain portion of the playlist to a specific "
"value, such as Artist, Composer, Title, Genre, Year, &etc; You can specify "
"as many biases as you like to work together. This is a very flexible way of "
"choosing your playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Don't be confused, though -- a dynamic playlist containing the following two "
"biases: 50% Artist: Michael Jackson, 50% Genre:Rock can contain tracks that "
"are from neither Michael Jackson nor have a Rock genre. This is because "
"while both biases are used, half the time a track will be chosen which is "
"Jackson, and half the time not, and the same for Rock. So if you want 50/50 "
"Jackson and Rock, set the biases to 100% for each."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5332
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Bias"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where you will find the new Last.fm and Echo Nest biases. Use Last."
"fm or Echo Nest to bias the playlist towards artists who are similar to "
"either the currently playing artist, your weekly top artists in Last.fm; or "
"for Echo Nest, the current playlist as a whole."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This function will use as a seed whatever song is playing when the playlist "
"is repopulated so your music evolves as you listen, while remaining somewhat "
"similar to whatever is currently playing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5338
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fuzzy Bias"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fuzzy bias will match an approximate value and has a strictness field, as "
"opposed to a percentage one. More strictness means more exact matches. The "
"resulting playlist will consist of tracks normally distributed around the "
"requested value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using your Dynamic Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enable the dynamic playlist you have created simply check the "
"<guilabel>On</guilabel> box in the upper-left corner of the pane. To "
"regenerate the entire playlist at any time, click <guilabel>Repopulate</"
"guilabel>, to the right of <guilabel>On</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default number of items in the playlist is your 5 previous plays plus 10 "
"upcoming items. With the currently playing track, this makes 16 items in the "
"playlist at any given time. The number of tracks can be changed right below "
"the <guilabel>On</guilabel> checkbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below that are is the dropdown menu for loading saved playlists, the "
"<guilabel>Save</guilabel> button, and the <guilabel>Delete</guilabel> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5367
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Playlist Generator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Automated Playlist Generator (APG)</emphasis> automatically "
"generates playlists based on constraints you set. These constraints can be "
"set based on song data (Author, Artist, Genre) or access time (Last Time "
"Played). There are also special constraints to determine how &amarok; is "
"going to look for songs. You will find the <emphasis>APG</emphasis> in your "
"<emphasis>Media</emphasis> pane, <menuchoice><guimenu>Playlists</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Automated Playlist Generator</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5370
#, no-c-format
msgid "APG Presets Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5384
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the <emphasis>APG Presets</emphasis> toolbar. From left to right we "
"have the following buttons:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add new preset: Adds a blank preset that can be modified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5388
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Edit selected preset: Opens up the <emphasis>APG Preset Editor</emphasis> "
"window to edit the currently selected preset constraints."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Delete selected preset: Removes the selected preset from the list; can "
"<guilabel>NOT</guilabel> be undone."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Import new preset: Import a preset from a .xml file. Has the potential to be "
"malformed if edited outside &amarok;; use the constraint tester."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Export the selected preset: Export the selected preset to a .xml file that "
"can be imported."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Run constraint tester: Tests the selected preset for consistency."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Run <emphasis>APG</emphasis> with selected preset: Loads <emphasis>APG</"
"emphasis> with the selected preset and automatically generates a playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working with Presets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:5405
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>APG Preset Editor window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5408
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>APG Preset Editor window</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Presets are sets of rules that &amarok; <emphasis>APG</emphasis> will use "
"when generating playlists. These rules are going to be referred to as "
"<emphasis>constraints</emphasis> from now on; every preset is determined by "
"the constraints which create it. Groups of constraints hierarchically and "
"logically organized are called constraint trees."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Constraints"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Constraints are the building blocks of constraint trees. They are simple "
"statements that the <emphasis>APG</emphasis> will use to add songs to the "
"playlist it generates To add a constraint to the currently selected preset "
"constraint tree use the <guilabel>Edit selected preset</guilabel> option "
"from the <emphasis>APG Preset toolbar</emphasis> and click the <guilabel>Add "
"new</guilabel> option on the <emphasis>APG Preset Editor</emphasis> window. "
"Note that this will add the constraint under the selected item (constraint "
"or constraint group)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5418
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many different kinds of constraints can be added; each works in a different "
"way inside the tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Constraint Types"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; <emphasis>APG</emphasis> supports several types of constraints:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:5429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Constraint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:5436
#, no-c-format
msgid "Match Tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most important constraints, because they can be set to virtually any "
"information regarding the file, including: artist name, album name, genre, "
"year, last time played, bpm, sample rate and score."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:5444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist Duration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5447
#, no-c-format
msgid "Set the running time (in HH:MM:SS format) that the playlist should have"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:5452
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist Length"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5455
#, no-c-format
msgid "Determine how many songs should be in the playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:5460
#, no-c-format
msgid "Checkpoint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5463
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tell &amarok; where to start and stop looking for tracks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:5468
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prevent Duplicates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5471
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Prevent &amarok; from selecting the same tracks, songs from the same artist, "
"or the same album"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that you can change how constraints work in various manners, such as "
"setting the fuzzy-exact slider, which determines how closely the constraint "
"is going to be followed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5479
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another way to modify constraints that is present mainly on <guilabel>Match "
"Tags</guilabel> is the option box at the left of the value to: "
"<guilabel>contains</guilabel> (which will consider any songs that have the "
"according text in their tag), <guilabel>matches</guilabel> (which will "
"consider songs whose corresponding match exactly the one in the text box), "
"<guilabel>starts with</guilabel> and <guilabel>ends with</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5481
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also edit the way value-based (such as the Length constraints and "
"the playcount <guilabel>Match Tag</guilabel> constraint) behave by changing "
"the option close to the text to settings such as <guilabel>fewer than</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>equals</guilabel> and <guilabel>more than</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another way to change constraint behavior is to check the <guilabel>invert</"
"guilabel> checkbox on them, this makes them behave the opposite way, a "
"<emphasis>Match Tag: artist contains</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5486
#, no-c-format
msgid "Constraint Groups"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Constraint groups can be added from the <guilabel>Add new</guilabel> option "
"from the <emphasis>APG Preset Editor</emphasis> window, constraints under a "
"group are logically linked, the same applies to groups under groups."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5489
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are currently two kinds of constraint groups: <quote>Match all</quote> "
"groups and <quote>Match any</quote> groups. <quote>Match all</quote> groups "
"require that all the constraints under them are met by the song. "
"<quote>Match any</quote> groups require that at least one of the constraints "
"under them are met by the song. To add a constraint under a specific group "
"highlight it on the preset editor and use the <guilabel>Add new</guilabel> "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5493
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using your Presets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you set up a preset, you just have to select it on the <emphasis>APG "
"Presets</emphasis> panel and click the rightmost button on the toolbar, "
"<guilabel>Run APG with selected preset</guilabel>. You will then have a "
"playlist matching your criteria, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:5504
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Playlist generated by the constraint tree below.</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5507
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Playlist generated by the constraint tree below.</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5528
#, no-c-format
msgid "Various"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Topics which didn't fit elsewhere, such a Moodbar, Amarok on other "
"platforms, troubleshooting, common problems, and the FAQ:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5532
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"the-moodbar\">Moodbar</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"amarok-on-other-platforms\">Amarok on other Desktops and "
"Operating Systems</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5534 index.docbook:5826
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"amarok-on-non-kde-desktops\">Non-KDE Desktops</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5535
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"amarok-on-windows\">Amarok on Windows</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5536
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"amarok-on-mac-os-x\">Amarok on OS X</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"troubleshooting-and-common-problems\">Troubleshooting and "
"Common Problems</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5540
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"frequently-asked-questions\">FAQ</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5542
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Moodbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Moodbar</emphasis> officially returns as of &amarok; 2.2.2. It "
"shows you the <quote>mood</quote> of a track, which you can then use to "
"figure out when something interesting happens in the song."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order for &amarok; to analyze your music files to create moodbars, you "
"will need the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> program (see below for <link "
"linkend=\"source-downloads\">downloads</link> and binary packages)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> package requires <emphasis>GStreamer</"
"emphasis> and various plugins depending on the filetypes you use (see <link "
"linkend=\"supported-filetypes\">Supported filetypes</link>). You will "
"<guilabel>not</guilabel> need the phonon-backend-gstreamer package to "
"create .mood files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5549
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two parts to the new <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> implementation: "
"the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> package, which contains a program that "
"takes a music file and generates a .mood file, and support code in the "
"&amarok; source, which runs the binary and displays the Moodbar. The "
"<guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> package depends on the <emphasis>GStreamer</"
"emphasis> libraries. Without the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> package, "
"Amarok cannot generate the moodbars for your music."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As an alternative, there is a new script which will create moodbar files for "
"tracks in an &amarok; playlist; this is an exception to the above. The "
"script needs nothing but Amarok to work, but it only creates the .mood files "
"as they are played in the <emphasis>Playlist</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5553
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Moodbar</emphasis> is due to the work of Gavin Wood and Simon "
"O'Keefe, who designed the algorithms; their original paper is <ulink url="
"\"http://cratoo.de/amarok/ismir-crc.pdf\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5555
#, no-c-format
msgid "Summary of Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> binary, in your PATH (it should be listed "
"upon running <userinput>which moodbar</userinput> from a console) -- "
"Remember to configure the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> package with "
"<userinput>./configure --prefix=`pkg-config --variable=prefix "
"gstreamer-0.10`</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>GStreamer</emphasis> 0.10 library and <link linkend="
"\"supported-filetypes\">plugins</link> for the formats you want "
"<guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> to be able to analyse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5559
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <emphasis>Fastest Fourier Transform In The West</emphasis> (http://www."
"fftw.org) <emphasis>FFTW</emphasis> library version 3.0 or above (at least "
"single-precision floating point version - libfftw3f) -- If your platform "
"does not provide this for you or you need to compile your own version, "
"remember to configure the <emphasis>FFTW</emphasis> package with "
"<userinput>./configure --enable-single</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A version of &amarok; with a <guilabel>Use moods</guilabel> option in the "
"General section of the configuration screen. This means 1.4.4 or higher in "
"the 1.4 series or 2.2.2 or higher in the 2.x series."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Systems with package managers should automatically install the "
"<emphasis>GStreamer</emphasis> plugins and <emphasis>FFTW</emphasis> along "
"with <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel>; this information is provided mostly for "
"people who want or need to compile from source xor manually install packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5565
#, no-c-format
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently .mood files must generated manually. To do this for your entire "
"collection, use the <link linkend=\"moodbar-file-generation-script\">Moodbar "
"File Generation Script</link> described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5568
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enable the display of moodbars in &amarok;, activate it in the "
"configuration: <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Configure "
"Amarok</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>General</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Show "
"Moodbar in Progress Slider</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Moodbars should now "
"appear in the track sliders in the player window and the playlist window; "
"there will also be a mood field that you may add to your playlist layouts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5571 index.docbook:6209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5572
#, no-c-format
msgid "Source Downloads"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Latest release: <ulink url=\"http://pwsp.net/~qbob/moodbar-0.1.2.tar.gz"
"\">moodbar-0.1.2.tar.gz</ulink> -- this is the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> "
"source package, which contains the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> program "
"(which generates .mood files from music files), and a <emphasis>GStreamer</"
"emphasis> plugin that does the work. The <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> "
"package needs <emphasis>GStreamer</emphasis> 0.10.* installed, plus the 0.10."
"* version of <link linkend=\"supported-filetypes\">various plugins</link>. "
"Be sure to install the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> package into the "
"<guilabel>same prefix</guilabel> as <emphasis>GStreamer</emphasis> -- follow "
"the instructions in the INSTALL file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you find any bugs, please submit a bug report at <ulink url=\"http://bugs."
"kde.org\">bugs.kde.org</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5578
#, no-c-format
