#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5666
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moodbar File Generation Script"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5667
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here is a simple bash script that will add .mood files to your entire "
"collection. It adds mood files for all files matching the extensions in the "
"current directory and all subdirectories, so it's best run from the base of "
"your music directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:5669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#!/bin/bash\n"
" DIR=${1:-.}\n"
" LAST=~/.moodbar-lastreadsong\n"
" C_RET=0\n"
" control_c()        # run if user hits control-c\n"
" {\n"
"   echo \"\" &gt; \"$LAST\"\n"
"   echo \"Exiting...\"\n"
"   exit\n"
" }\n"
" if [ -e \"$LAST\" ]; then\n"
"   read filetodelete &lt; \"$LAST\"\n"
"   rm \"$filetodelete\" \"$LAST\"\n"
" fi\n"
" exec 9&lt; &lt;(find \"$DIR\" -type f -regextype posix-awk -iregex '.*\\."
"(mp3|ogg|flac|wma)') # you may need to add m4a and mp4\n"
" while read i\n"
" do\n"
"   TEMP=\"${i%.*}.mood\"\n"
"   OUTF=`echo \"$TEMP\" | sed 's#\\(.*\\)/\\([^,]*\\)#\\1/.\\2#'`\n"
"   trap 'control_c \"$OUTF\"' INT\n"
"   if [ ! -e \"$OUTF\" ]\n"
"     moodbar -o \"$OUTF\" \"$i\"\n"
"   fi\n"
" done &lt;&amp;9\n"
" exec 9&lt;&amp;-\n"
" exit $C_RET"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5671
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copy and paste the above into a text file named moodbar.sh in your music "
"directory and run the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:5673
#, no-c-format
msgid "cd /path/to/music bash moodbar.sh"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5678
#, no-c-format
msgid "Alternatively if the above does not work, you may try:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:5680
#, no-c-format
msgid "chmod +x moodbar.sh ./moodbar.sh"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This may take a very long time for large collections! Note that the moodbars "
"will not appear in Amarok until Amarok rescans the collection. The generated "
"mood files will be dotfiles (ie, prefixed with a full stop), or hidden files "
"- so keep this in mind if you can't find any generated mood files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5687
#, no-c-format
msgid "Based on the above script, an alternative for multicore CPUs:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:5689
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#!/bin/bash\n"
" NUMCPU=\"$(grep ^processor /proc/cpuinfo | wc -l)\"\n"
" find . -type f -regextype posix-awk -iregex '.*\\.(mp3|ogg|flac|wma)' | "
"while read i ; do\n"
"        while [ `jobs -p | wc -l` -ge $NUMCPU ] ; do\n"
"                sleep 0.1\n"
"        done\n"
"        TEMP=\"${i%.*}.mood\"\n"
"        OUTF=`echo \"$TEMP\" | sed 's#\\(.*\\)/\\([^,]*\\)#\\1/.\\2#'`\n"
"        if [ ! -e \"$OUTF\" ] ; then\n"
"                moodbar -o \"$OUTF\" \"$i\" &amp;\n"
"        fi\n"
" done"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5691
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is another script at <ulink url=\"https://github.com/aendruk/moodbar-"
"preview-cli\">Github</ulink>, which shows previews of the generated mood "
"files on the command line while they are being generated. Read more about it "
"at the <ulink url=\"https://aendruk.wordpress.com/2011/02/13/moodbar-"
"previews-on-the-command-line/\">author's blog</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:5694 index.docbook:6381
#, no-c-format
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> executable gives you a <emphasis>bus "
"error</emphasis>, that almost always means it can't decode (or can't find) "
"your file. Take a look at the <link linkend=\"supported-filetypes"
"\">supported file types</link> below for ideas on which <emphasis>GStreamer</"
"emphasis> plugins to install. You can also try the command below to test "
"whether <emphasis>GStreamer</emphasis> can decode your file:<userinput>gst-"
"launch filesrc location=[file] ! decodebin ! fakesink</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5697
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are using the ffmpeg plugin to decode mp3s, you may also receive "
"mysterious bus errors. The solution is to stop using the ffmpeg plugin, as "
"it is extremely buggy -- use mad instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5698
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> executable tells you that it can't find "
"an element -- i.e, it gives an error message like"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:5698
#, no-c-format
msgid "Could not create element of type fftwspectrum, please install it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5700
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"-- that usually means that you either don't have the required plugins "
"installed (see the plugin list <link linkend=\"supported-filetypes\">here</"
"link>), or that you didn't install the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> package "
"in the same prefix as <emphasis>GStreamer</emphasis>. If libmoodbar.so and "
"libgstdecodebin.so are not in the same directory, then <guilabel>Moodbar</"
"guilabel> is not installed in the same prefix as <emphasis>GStreamer</"
"emphasis>. Please read the INSTALL file for instructions on how to configure "
"the moodbar package correctly. Alternatively, <emphasis>if you know what "
"you're doing,</emphasis> it may be easier for you to take a look at the "
"<filename>GST_PLUGIN_PATH</filename> environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5703
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you're wondering why the <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> isn't working, "
"either not working at all or not working for a particular file, run the "
"command below, where [file] is a music file:<userinput>moodbar -o test.mood "
"[file]</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:5704
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have multiple versions of <emphasis>GStreamer</emphasis> installed, "
"make sure all of the required plugins are installed <guilabel>for version "
"0.10.*</guilabel> -- different versions <emphasis>cannot</emphasis> use each "
"other's plugins."
