"wiki/Amarok2_On_OS_X\">troubleshooting page here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Troubleshooting and Common Problems"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you work through the procedures here, but don't have success, please come "
"into IRC (irc://irc.freenode.org/amarok), post on the KDE Forum <ulink url="
"\"http://forum.kde.org/viewforum.php?f=127\">Amarok section</ulink>, or "
"write to the <ulink url=\"https://mail.kde.org/mailman/listinfo/amarok"
"\">Amarok list</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Problems installing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bad packaging"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Occasionally, users will encounter bad packaging from the distributions; "
"either from the wrong version of a component being included, or some needful "
"part being left out. For some reason, this often happens with MySQL "
"dependencies. Bug reports in these cases should be made to your "
"distribution, not to bugs.kde.org."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Difficulties building from source"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For those who wish to help out by testing the newest &amarok; versions, a "
"local build is advised. Use this excellent guide: <ulink url=\"http://blogs."
"fsfe.org/myriam/2009/09/compiling-amarok-from-git-locally-full-summary/"
"\">Compiling &amarok; from GIT Locally; a Full Summary</ulink>. Detailed "
"information about git can be found here: <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde."
"org/Getting_Started/Sources/KDE_git-tutorial\">Techbase GIT Tutorial</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have built successfully before, and now are encountering errors, try "
"removing <emphasis>CMakeCache.txt</emphasis> and try again. If that still "
"errors out, remove the entire Build folder and build completely fresh."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The URL to pull from git has recently changed. Run <userinput>git remote set-"
"url origin git://anongit.kde.org/amarok</userinput> if you still using the "
"old URL. Please ping us if you find the old link in our documents so we can "
"update it everywhere."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6128
#, no-c-format
msgid "Problems starting up"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist errors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The current playlist can occasionally get corrupt, which will prevent "
"&amarok; from starting. This can be fixed by simply removing the current "
"playlist file in the &amarok; directory, $HOME/.kde/share/apps/amarok/"
"current.xspf . Note that on some systems, this may be .kde4 rather than .kde."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Database issues"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the database is corrupt and this is preventing &amarok; from starting, "
"you can move the database to a backup location (or simply delete it). This "
"will cause &amarok; to rebuild the database from scratch. Move the $HOME/."
"kde/share/apps/amarok/mysqle folder to a backup location (such as $HOME/.kde/"
"share/apps/amarok/mysqle~) and restart &amarok;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6137
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other issues and backing up settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the above two items do not help, or you otherwise need to restore "
"&amarok; to a clean configuration, you can move to a backup location (or "
"delete) the &amarok; directory at $HOME/.kde/share/apps/amarok and the "
"&amarok; config files at $HOME/.kde/share/config/amarok* (there may be two "
"or three files matching this pattern). Again, the directory may be .kde4 "
"rather than .kde."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Problems Scanning, Sorting files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; scans your music files on first startup, and will keep your "
"collection up-to-date automatically, if you chose "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Configure Amarok</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Collection</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Watch folders "
"for changes</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't want &amarok; scanning for changes, uncheck that, and use "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Update Collection</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> whenever you make changes to your collection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More about <link linkend=\"collection-scanning\">&amarok; collection "
"scanning here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Corrupt tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some folks notice that &amarok; seems to be missing some files. One of the "
"causes can be corrupt tags, which you can check using the tagging "
"application <ulink url=\"http://kid3.sourceforge.net/\">kid3</ulink>. More "
"about tagging <link linkend=\"tag-editor\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To find the bad file(s), run <emphasis>amarokcollectionscanner</emphasis> "
"from the console. Details <ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/wiki/Batch_Mode"
"\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inability to write tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &amarok; is not saving changes to tags, you may have permissions "
"problems. Ensure that your user has write permissions to your music. For "
"example, <userinput>chown -R youruser Music/</userinput> to change ownership "
"to your user, or <userinput>chmod -R +w Music/</userinput> to add write "
"permissions to the owner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Incorrect Sorting (Various Artists)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes people report that tracks are in Various Artists when they should "
"not be, or are sorted into <quote>Unknown Album.</quote> What separates "
"Various Artists albums and tracks and albums sorted under their artists is "
"the Album Artist tag. When you click <guilabel>Show under Various Artists</"
"guilabel> in the context (right-click) menu, that tag will be emptied if it "
"is filled. The opposite happens to a file in Various Artists when you choose "
"<guilabel>Do not show under Various Artists</guilabel>, but the Album Artist "
"tag will be auto-filled from the Artist tag."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is no Album tag, and no Album Artist tag, &amarok; will put the "
"track into Unknown Album in Various Artists. If you want them sorted "
"otherwise, tag them the way you want them sorted. If you don't know some of "
"the information, try out the new <emphasis>MusicBrainz</emphasis> function "
"in the tag editor, or use a tagging application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6166
#, no-c-format
msgid "Problems playing files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amarok skips over tracks, or appears to play them without sound"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the files you are attempting to play are in mp3 format, please see "
"instructions for enabling mp3 support on your distro, <link linkend=\"what-"
"media-types-does-amarok-support\">here</link>. Note that one piece of "
"software being able to play mp3s on your system does not necessarily mean "
"&amarok; has had the required codecs installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6171
#, no-c-format
msgid "No sound, or bad sound"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more general sound issues, first check what Phonon backend you are using "
"in <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Configure Amarok</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Playback</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Configure Phonon</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Backend</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Consider "
"switching to a different backend; VLC, GStreamer and Xine backends should be "
"available from your distribution, although Xine is deprecated. Gstreamer or "
"VLC is usually recommended."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Also check whether the backend standalone software can play the files "
"correctly; if not this is an issue with that software and you may find "
"information in their help files. In other words, can Gstreamer or VLC play "
"the same file? Will it play in <ulink url=\"help:/dragonplayer\">Dragon</"
"ulink>, which also uses phonon?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If it seems to be a PulseAudio problem, and you want to provide a log to the "
"PulseAudio developers, the troubleshooting page is <ulink url=\"https://wiki."
"ubuntu.com/PulseAudio/Log\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Crashes and bugs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How to run &amarok; from the command line: <userinput>amarok --debug --"
"nofork</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; crashes, but <guilabel>Dr. Konqi</guilabel> doesn't pop up -- run "
"in <guilabel>gdb</guilabel> with the following command: <userinput>gdb --"
"args amarok --debug --nofork</userinput> In gdb's console, type "
"<emphasis>run</emphasis> to start &amarok;, reproduce the crash, and then in "
"gdb type <emphasis>thread apply all bt</emphasis> to generate the backtrace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Filing bugs: If triggered, Dr. Konqi will provide an option to report a bug "
"and do most of the work for you. If not, you will need to submit the bug "
"manually at <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org/enter_bug.cgi?product=amarok\"> "
"bugs.kde.org</ulink>. For crash bugs, paste the backtrace from gdb as a "
"comment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How to get personal support with problems: <ulink url=\"irc://irc.freenode."
"net/#amarok\">IRC</ulink> (#amarok on Freenode IRC), <ulink url=\"http://"
"forum.kde.org/viewforum.php?f=127\">Forum</ulink>, <ulink url=\"https://mail."
"kde.org/mailman/listinfo/amarok\">Mailing list</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently Asked Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6190
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is Amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; is a music player. More information can be found in <link linkend="
"\"amarok-menu\">a summary of its features</link> and the <ulink url=\"http://"
"amarok.kde.org/en/screenshots\">screenshot gallery</ulink>. To get started "
"using &amarok;, see the <link linkend=\"quick-start-guide\"><emphasis>Quick "
"Start Guide</emphasis></link>. The <guilabel>Amarok Handbook</guilabel> is "
"<link linkend=\"introduction\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6194
#, no-c-format
msgid "What are the differences between Amarok 2 and the previous versions?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; 2 is a nearly complete code-rewrite so the codebase has little to "
"do with &amarok; 1.4. If you are missing a feature, please file a wish in "
"<ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org\">Bugzilla</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you have a short list of some new features:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Maybe the biggest new feature is the <emphasis>Service Framework</emphasis>, "
"which integrates networked music sources directly into &amarok;. This "
"includes online music stores, media servers, Web music lockers, and more. "
"Thanks to it you'll get easy access to music provided by "
"<emphasis>Magnatune</emphasis>, <emphasis>Jamendo</emphasis>, <emphasis>Last."
"fm</emphasis>, <emphasis>MP3Tunes Locker</emphasis>, <guilabel>Ampache</"
"guilabel> and many others. Expect more big (and small) names to join during "
"the 2.x lifecycle. See <link linkend=\"internet\">Internet Media Sources</"
"link> for more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another exciting feature is the <emphasis>Context</emphasis> pane, occupying "
"the central place of the &amarok;<command>'s</command> window, replacing the "
"old <emphasis>Context Browser</emphasis> from the 1.x series. It displays "
"contextual information about the music you play, like the album cover, track "
"rating, labels, lyrics, artist information, related songs and artists, "
"guitar and bass tabs and others. Thanks to the Plasma technology it uses, "
"the <emphasis>Context</emphasis> pane can provide very rich content, like "
"AJAX, video and animations, all in an eye-catching fashion. More about the "
"<link linkend=\"the-context-pane\">Context pane</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To accompany the <emphasis>Context</emphasis> pane, we developed a new, "
"space efficient playlist. In order to preserve horizontal space, it groups "
"the track name, artist, album name and cover art together, and allows "
"further grouping by album names. Plus you can rearrange it to your heart's "
"content! If you prefer the old 1.4 playlist, you can have that too. See "
"<link linkend=\"changing-the-playlist-layout\">Changing the Playlist layout</"
"link> for more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another great gem is the video support. Watching your music videos inside "
"&amarok; feels great!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We can't forget the <emphasis>Dynamic Playlists</emphasis>, which extend the "
"old <emphasis>Dynamic Playlists</emphasis>. They allow you to define an "
"automatically populated playlist, based on specific probability driven "
"criteria called <quote>biases</quote>. The dynamic playlist is joined by the "
"new Automatic Playlist Generator, used to generate lists for specific "
"purposes and of a specified length. See <link linkend=\"dynamic-playlists"
"\">Dynamic Playlists</link> and <link linkend=\"automatic-playlist-generator"
"\">Automatic Playlist Generator</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are many more great features like advanced scripting, dynamic "
"collections, usability improvements, improved media devices handling, a new "
"podcast manager, support for more software platforms, and others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use Amarok without KDE?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; requires parts of KDE to be installed to run, but will run fine in "
"Gnome or other desktop environments, including Windows and OSx. For &amarok; "
"to run, kdelibs and kdebase-runtime need to be installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For some features to work correctly, such as the on-screen display, your "
"window manager must be configured to support the relevant "
"<emphasis>freedesktop.org</emphasis> standards. More about running &amarok; "
"on other platforms <link linkend=\"amarok-on-other-platforms\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why does Amarok use KDElibs?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We are committed to supporting &amarok; on all platforms. We use KDElibs and "
"Qt because they provide an excellent development environment. Aside from "
"&Linux; and BSD, &amarok; works on Windows and MacOS, and there are "
"installers available, but unfortunately we don't have (yet) the resources to "
"offer full support for those operating systems. Almost all of our developers "
"use free operating systems, and those have priority for us. We do however "
"welcome Windows and OS X developers willing to help, and improve &amarok; on "
"those platforms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6221
#, no-c-format
msgid "General usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6222
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I control Amarok from the keyboard?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keyboard shortcuts are available; see our <link linkend=\"keybinding-"
"reference\">Keybinding Reference page</link> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To control &amarok; from the console, type <userinput>amarok --help-all</"
"userinput> for a current complete list of available control commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get support for Amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are several options. Often times problems you have with the initial "
"install of &amarok; are best answered by experts of your particular &UNIX; "
"or &Linux; distribution. You may seek help from fellow users and developers "
"at the <ulink url=\"http://forum.kde.org/viewforum.php?f=127\">&amarok; "
"forum</ulink> and the <ulink url=\"irc://irc.freenode.net/amarok\">&amarok; "
"IRC channel</ulink> at irc.freenode.net channel #amarok."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org\">bugzilla</ulink> is not a place "
"to seek support. Please do enter a bug if you are serious about helping fix "
"a bug in &amarok; itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions about the Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More about the <link linkend=\"the-playlist-pane\">Playlist here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I start Amarok, I see an empty playlist. How do I actually get tracks "
"in there?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <emphasis>Collection</emphasis> on the left side to navigate to the "
"desired artist/album/track. Then drag the files into the <emphasis>Playlist</"
"emphasis> part on the right. You can use <emphasis>Dynamic Playlists</"
"emphasis> or the <emphasis>Automatic Playlist Generator</emphasis> to "
"populate your playlist. You can also drag files in from any file manager, "
"such as <guilabel>Dolphin</guilabel>. You may also double-click a track, "
"artist or genre in your <emphasis>Collection</emphasis> or file-system, or "
"right-click and <guilabel>Add to Playlist</guilabel> or <guilabel>Replace "
"Playlist</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6242
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I remove tracks from the Playlist?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the track(s) you want to remove, and press the <keycap>Delete</"
"keycap> key. Or right-click the selection and choose <guilabel>Remove From "
"Playlist</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6246
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I load a playlist?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just drag and drop the playlist file into the <emphasis>Playlist</emphasis>, "
"like you would do with any other file. It's that simple!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6250
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I save the current playlist?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <guilabel>Save Playlist As</guilabel> button in the "
"<emphasis>Playlist</emphasis> toolbar. Slow-click the disc icon to chose to "
"save to your harddisk, or to the database."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6255
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playback Questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6256
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I play audio CDs?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you insert an audio CD, it will be shown as a local collection. Drag to "
"the playlist or <emphasis>Pop-Up Dropper</emphasis>, or right-click the "
"selected tracks and choose <guilabel>Add to Playlist</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Replace Playlist</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6260
#, no-c-format
msgid "What media types does Amarok support?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; does not play music by itself, but lets <emphasis>Phonon</emphasis> "
"do that job, specifically the <emphasis>VLC</emphasis>, <emphasis>GStreamer</"
"emphasis> or <emphasis>Xine backends</emphasis> of <emphasis>Phonon</"
"emphasis>. Therefore, whatever files they can play, &amarok; can play. To "
"analyse file tags, &amarok; uses <emphasis>Taglib</emphasis>, which supports "
"most file types that contain metadata."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6264
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is Phonon? What are Phonon backends?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Phonon</emphasis> is the multimedia framework of KDE 4. You can "
"find more information <link linkend=\"playback\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually the <emphasis>VLC backend</emphasis> works better than the "
"<emphasis>Xine</emphasis> one, although this is not always true. We also "
"suggest you try the <emphasis>Gstreamer backend</emphasis>, although it is "
"still in development. You can find more details on installing backends in "
"the <ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/wiki/Download\">download page</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6270
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amarok won't play mp3s, what can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6271
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Have a look at the <ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/wiki/MP3\">mp3 "
"information page</ulink>. You probably lack the codecs required by your "
"particular <emphasis>phonon-backend</emphasis> (<guilabel>VLC,</guilabel> "
"<guilabel>Gstreamer</guilabel>, or <guilabel>Xine</guilabel>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6274
#, no-c-format
msgid "I can't get any media to play in Amarok, why not?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Test the sound frameworks at the command line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:6277
#, no-c-format
msgid "xine-check"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(The <emphasis>xine-ui</emphasis> package contains <guilabel>xine-check</"
"guilabel>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The output from these commands should help you identify the problems you are "
"having and how to fix them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I have a second soundcard and I'm using ALSA. How do I make Amarok use it "
"instead of the default?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Configure this in the <emphasis>Phonon</emphasis> system settings module. "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Configure Amarok</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Playback</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Configure Phonon</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where's the equalizer?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The equalizer is only available if you are using a <emphasis>Phonon</"
"emphasis>-backend which supports it, which the modern ones now do. You can "
"find it in the <guilabel>Tools</guilabel> menu. You can get more information "
"about configuring <emphasis>Phonon</emphasis>-backends in your distribution "
"in the <ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/wiki/Download\">download page</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6292
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I turn on visualizations?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Visualizations are not implemented yet, but they will be very soon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6296
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I add podcasts?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Go to <emphasis>Podcast</emphasis> section in the left toolbar and then "
"select <guilabel>Add Podcast...</guilabel> Add the podcast URL where "
"indicated. More about podcasts <link linkend=\"podcasts\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We also have some services, such as gpodder and Podcast Directory to help "
"you find great podcasts. Enable services in the <guilabel>Settings</"
"guilabel> menu: <menuchoice><guimenu>Configure Amarok</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Plugins</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6302
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I use Amarok to stream to my own radio station?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to stream directly to an icecast or shoutcast server the answer "
"simply is: it is not supported. You could use <ulink url=\"http://giss.tv/"
"sahabuntu/doc/idjc.html\">IDJC</ulink> for that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6307
#, no-c-format
msgid "General questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6308
#, no-c-format
msgid "What are scripts?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"They are little pieces of software that add some functions to &amarok;. "
"There are a lot of scripts, and you can find them in <ulink url=\"http://www."
"kde-apps.org/index.php?xcontentmode=57\">kde-apps.org</ulink> or you can "
"find and install them inside &amarok; using the <emphasis>Script Manager</"
"emphasis> (until &amarok; 2.4.1). More details <link linkend=\"script-manager"
"\">here</link>. After &amarok; 2.4.1, you will find the Script Manager from "
"the <guilabel>Settings</guilabel> menu, <menuchoice><guimenu>Configure "
"Amarok</guimenu><guimenuitem>Scripts</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6312
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use Amarok 1.4 scripts in Amarok 2?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No. A new and powerful scripting API has been created, which provides huge "
"improvements but won't let you use your old scripts. The new scripting "
"system is based on QtScript and will significantly reduce &amarok;"
"<command>'s</command> dependencies, a huge problem for non-technical and "
"cross-platform users, and will greatly reduce the amount of external "
"processes launched at runtime. Another advantage is that the new API will "
"allow much deeper integration with &amarok; than the old scripting system. "
"<ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/wiki/Development/Script_API\">Amarok "
"Scripting API</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6316
#, no-c-format
msgid "What are Moodbars?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Moodbars</emphasis> show the mood of a song in the progress bar. "
"More about <guilabel>Moodbar</guilabel> <link linkend=\"the-moodbar\">here</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6320
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I play video files?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; is mainly a music player so no video file management, collection "
"support, DVD playback, subtitles, or any other sophisticated features are "
"available. However, the <emphasis>video applet</emphasis> lets you play "
"YouTube video clips inside &amarok;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6324
#, no-c-format
msgid "Is it Amarok, AmaroK or amaroK?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is &amarok;! The former spelling was <emphasis>amaroK</emphasis>, but it "
"was changed due to its strange look."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6328
#, no-c-format
msgid "How are track scores determined?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; assigns a score (a number 0-100) to a song based on how many times "
"you've listened to it and whether you skip the song without it finishing. "
"Every time the song finishes playing, the score is changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you have an example script that can calculate scores:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6333
#, no-c-format
msgid "if( playcount &lt;= 0 ) # not supposed to be less, but what the hell."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6335
#, no-c-format
msgid "newscore = ( prevscore + percentage ) / 2"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6337
#, no-c-format
msgid "else"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"newscore = ( ( prevscore * playcount ) + percentage ) / ( playcount + 1 )"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6341
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>end</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can easily create your own script with your own algorithm. Look at the "
"<ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/wiki/Development/"
"Scripting_HowTo_2.0\">Script-Writing-Howto</ulink> for further information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6346
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I manually change a track's score?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may change the score manually in the <emphasis>Edit Track Details</"
"emphasis> dialog, available by right-clicking on a track, and choosing the "
"<guilabel>Summary</guilabel> tab. Before &amarok; 2.4.1, this is called the "
"<guilabel>Statistics</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6350
#, no-c-format
msgid "But I also want that stars system like in other players!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok;, of course, supports an user-defined rating system, and you can "
"rate your tracks with a single click using the <emphasis>Current Track "
"applet</emphasis>. You can also do this in the context menu (right-click) "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit Track Details</guimenu><guimenuitem>Summary</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> tab (before Amarok 2.4.1, this is "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit Track Details</guimenu><guimenuitem>Statistics</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>). If you have the rating stars displayed in your "
"playlist layout, you can also edit there, with the <emphasis>slow double-"
"click</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I drag and drop Plasma applets from the main window to the Desktop?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No, but there are many Plasmoids available for your Desktop, which will let "
"you display information provided by &amarok; as well as control &amarok;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6358
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use removable media inside Amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; has a greatly improved support for the media devices based on "
"<emphasis>Solid</emphasis>, the KDE hardware layer, that doesn't need a lot "
"of configuration. You should be able to just plug in your device and access "
"it within &amarok;. Also, thanks to the <emphasis>Dynamic Collections</"
"emphasis>, your media devices could become part of your music collection, "
"and be searchable and accessible within the <emphasis>Collection Browser</"
"emphasis> when it's connected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can transfer your songs, albums and artists from your local collection "
"by right-clicking <menuchoice><guimenu>Copy to Collection</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Your device</guimenuitem></menuchoice>; and you can "
"also do it in the other way: right-click <menuchoice><guimenu>Copy to "
"Collection</guimenu><guimenuitem>Local Collection</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>. More about &amarok; and devices <link linkend=\"working-with-"
"media-devices\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6364
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I save a stream?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First of all, load the stream into the playlist. There are several ways to "
"do this: downloading the file, for example from <ulink url=\"http://www."
"shoutcast.com\">shoutcast.com</ulink>, and opening it with &amarok;; using "
"the menu <menuchoice><guimenu>Playlist</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add stream</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>; among others."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6367
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the stream is loaded, you can save it by clicking on <guilabel>Save "
"current playlist</guilabel> which is under the Playlist, and giving it a "
"meaningful name. The Stream will then be added to the <emphasis>Saved "
"playlists view</emphasis> for later reference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Can I use the old Amarok's collection in Amarok 2? Will my tags, score are "
"ratings be lost?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A database importer is available. You will be able to keep your ratings and "
"statistics just fine. More <link linkend=\"collection\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where do I find the settings for Amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6375
#, no-c-format
msgid "`kde4-config --localprefix`/share/apps/amarok"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6377
#, no-c-format
msgid "`kde4-config --localprefix`/share/config/amarokrc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6382
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can I obtain a backtrace?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &amarok; has crashed and you want to report it, visit the <ulink url="
"\"http://amarok.kde.org/wiki/Debugging_(documentation)\">Debugging HowTo</"
"ulink>. The bug report must be sent in <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org"
"\">bugs.kde.org</ulink> after verifying if it has already been reported."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6386
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amarok just freezes! How can I help get this fixed?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can obtain a backtrace of a frozen instance of &amarok; using gdb like "
"so:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:6389
#, no-c-format
msgid "$ gdb -p `pidof amarok` (gdb) thread apply full bt all"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then just post the backtrace to <ulink url=\"http://paste.kde.org/"
"\">PasteBin</ulink>, as described in the <ulink url=\"http://amarok.kde.org/"
"wiki/Debugging_%28documentation%29\">Debugging HowTo</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6395
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amarok takes a lot of time to start"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this happens you have to check what scripts you have installed and what "
"internet services are running, because some of them may slow down the "
"startup. Also, if you have streams in the playlist when you open &amarok;, "
"the startup can take a little longer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if you don't use KDE, but a different desktop "
"environment, startup time can be increased very slightly because there are "
"more libraries to be loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6402
#, no-c-format
msgid "Development questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6403
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I get a GIT version of Amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/Getting_Started/Sources/KDE_git-tutorial"
"\">How to obtain and build &amarok; Git</ulink>. Check here for a local "
"build: <ulink url=\"http://blogs.fsfe.org/myriam/2009/09/compiling-amarok-"
"from-git-locally-full-summary/\">Building from Git Locally: Full Summary</"
"ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6407
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why isn't Amarok part of KDEmultimedia?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The developers don't want <emphasis>the man</emphasis> telling them when "
"they can release. (Meaning, packages in the KDE SC proper have a release "
"schedule that doesn't fit with &amarok;'s fast-paced development.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6411
#, no-c-format
msgid "I've found a bug / I've got a great idea for Amarok!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please report it at <ulink url=\"http://bugs.kde.org/enter_bug.cgi?"
"product=amarok\">bugs.kde.org</ulink>. If you have a list of suggestions or "
"wishes it may be best to send them to our mailing list: <ulink url=\"mailto:"
"amarok@kde.org\">amarok@kde.org</ulink>. Simply posting the idea to our IRC "
"channels or on an obscure wiki page or blog won't help much as the "
"information will get lost."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Do you accept patches?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Happily! Your best course of action is to let us know what you plan to do "
"before you do any work so we can discuss it, but don't fret; we haven't "
"turned down a patch yet! Discussion is mostly to help you patch the correct "
"bits of &amarok;. Submit your patches and code contributions to git."
"reviewboard.kde.org. See also <ulink url=\"http://blogs.fsfe.org/"
"myriam/2010/09/how-to-submit-patches-for-amarok/\">How to Submit Patches to "
"&amarok;</ulink>. If you have a bug fix then just go ahead; this is open "
"source after all. :)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:6419
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why did you choose the name Amarok?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:6420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Amarok</emphasis> is an album by British composer Mike Oldfield. "
"Project founder Mark Kretschmann happens to like it a lot, and he thought "
"the name had a nice sound. Plus, of course, it contains the all important "
"<guilabel>K</guilabel>. :)"
msgstr ""

